4) Documentation quality and notable inconsistencies (with evidence)

GitHub
- Add collaborator endpoint mentions “204 No Content” when updating a collaborator’s permission but 204 isn’t always explicitly listed in the responses table. Source — PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/collaborators/{username}
- /user/repos parameter interaction: using type together with visibility or affiliation yields a 422 error; this is clearly noted but easy to miss. Source — GET /user/repos
- Rate limit object deprecation: response includes both resources (preferred) and legacy rate fields; the spec calls out deprecation (can cause confusion if reading older examples). Source — GET /rate_limit
- Branch protection update uses both contexts (deprecated) and checks (preferred) structures; ensure teams/apps/users lists total ≤ 100 (hard limit). Source — PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection
- OAuth application token endpoints note “Authentication behaves differently” without detailing in the OpenAPI excerpt; implementers should follow the linked docs for the exact auth scheme. Source — POST/PATCH/DELETE /applications/{client_id}/token

