Endpoint: GET /user/repos
- Summary: List repositories for the authenticated user.
- Description: Lists repositories the authenticated user can explicitly access (:read, :write, or :admin) via:
  - Owned repositories
  - Collaborator repositories
  - Organization membership (incl. repos on teams the user is on)
- Tags: repos
- operationId: repos/list-for-authenticated-user
- External docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/repos/repos#list-repositories-for-the-authenticated-user

Query parameters
- visibility (string; default: all; enum: all, public, private)
  - Limit results to repos with the specified visibility.
- affiliation (string; default: owner,collaborator,organization_member)
  - Comma-separated values:
    - owner: repos owned by the user
    - collaborator: repos user is added to as collaborator
    - organization_member: repos user can access via org membership (incl. all team repos)
- type (string; default: all; enum: all, owner, public, private, member)
  - Limit by repo type; using with visibility or affiliation yields 422.
- sort (string; default: full_name; enum: created, updated, pushed, full_name)
- direction (string; enum: asc, desc; default asc when sort=full_name, otherwise desc)
- per_page (integer; default: 30; max: 100)
- page (integer; default: 1)
- since (string date-time, ISO 8601): only repos updated after this time
- before (string date-time, ISO 8601): only repos updated before this time
- Pagination docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/using-the-rest-api/using-pagination-in-the-rest-api

Responses
- 200 OK: application/json — array of Repository objects.

Repository (key properties)
- Identification/ownership
  - id (int64), node_id, name, full_name
