Endpoint: GET /rate_limit
- Summary: Get rate limit status for the authenticated user
- Notes:
  - Calling this endpoint does not count against REST API rate limits.
  - Some endpoint categories have separate/custom rate limits; response is categorized under resources.
  - Categories:
    - core (all non-search REST)
    - search (REST search, excluding code search)
    - code_search (REST code search)
    - graphql (GraphQL API)
    - integration_manifest (POST /app-manifests/{code}/conversions)
    - dependency_snapshots (submit snapshots to dependency graph)
    - dependency_sbom (request SBOMs from dependency graph)
    - code_scanning_upload (upload SARIF)
    - actions_runner_registration (register self-hosted runners)
    - scim
    - code_scanning_autofix
    - source_import (no longer used; will be removed next API version)
  - Deprecation notice: The rate object is being phased out; use core instead (same data).
- Tags: rate-limit
- OperationId: rate-limit/get
- Docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/rate-limit/rate-limit#get-rate-limit-status-for-the-authenticated-user
- Responses:
  - 200 application/json
    - Schema: object
      - resources: object
        - Each category listed above is a “Rate Limit” object with:
          - limit (integer), remaining (integer), reset (integer), used (integer)
          - Required: limit, remaining, reset, used
        - Required categories: core, search
      - rate: same “Rate Limit” object (deprecated in favor of core)
      - Required: rate, resources
    - Headers:
      - X-RateLimit-Limit: integer (e.g., 5000)
      - X-RateLimit-Remaining: integer (e.g., 4999)
      - X-RateLimit-Reset: integer timestamp (e.g., 1590701888)
  - 304 Not modified
  - 404 Resource not found
