Endpoint
- Path: POST /app/installations/{installation_id}/access_tokens
- OperationId: apps/create-installation-access-token
- Tag: apps
- Summary: Create an installation access token for a GitHub App
- External docs for method: https://docs.github.com/rest/apps/apps#create-an-installation-access-token-for-an-app

Behavior and constraints
- Creates a short-lived installation access token for a GitHub App installation on a user or org account.
- Token expiration: 1 hour from creation. Expired tokens return 401 Unauthorized; create a new token when expired.
- Repository access:
  - Default: token can access all repositories the installation has access to.
  - Optional scoping: use body parameters repositories (by name) or repository_ids (by ID) to limit access to specific repositories (max 500). Token cannot access repos outside the installation’s granted access.
- Permissions:
  - Optional: use permissions object in the request to limit granted permissions for the token.
  - If omitted: token inherits all permissions granted to the app.
  - You cannot grant permissions the app itself does not have.
- Authentication to call this endpoint: JWT as the GitHub App (authenticate as the app).

Path parameter
- installation_id (integer, required): Unique identifier of the installation.

Request body (application/json, optional)
- repositories: array of repository names (strings) to grant access to.
- repository_ids: array of repository IDs (integers) to grant access to.
- permissions (object): fine-grained permissions to grant. Unless otherwise noted, enums are read or write.
  - Repository-level: actions, administration, attestations, checks, codespaces, contents, dependabot_secrets, deployments, discussions, environments, issues, merge_queues, metadata, packages, pages, pull_requests, repository_custom_properties, repository_hooks, secret_scanning_alerts, secrets, security_events, single_file, statuses, vulnerability_alerts (all read/write); repository_projects (read/write/admin); workflows (write only).
  - Organization-level: custom_properties_for_organizations (read/write); members (read/write); organization_administration (read/write); organization_custom_roles (read/write); organization_custom_org_roles (read/write); organization_custom_properties (read/write/admin); organization_copilot_seat_management (write only); organization_announcement_banners (read/write); organization_events (read only); organization_hooks (read/write); organization_personal_access_tokens (read/write); organization_personal_access_token_requests (read/write); organization_plan (read only); organization_projects (read/write/admin); organization_packages (read/write); organization_secrets (read/write); organization_self_hosted_runners (read/write); organization_user_blocking (read/write); team_discussions (read/write).
  - User/enterprise-level: email_addresses (read/write); followers (read/write); git_ssh_keys (read/write); gpg_keys (read/write); interaction_limits (read/write); profile (write only); starring (read/write); enterprise_custom_properties_for_organizations (read/write/admin).

Response
- Status: 201 Created
- Content type: application/json
- Schema: Installation Token
  - token (string): the installation access token.
  - expires_at (string): token expiry timestamp.
  - permissions (object): effective permissions granted to the token (same shape as request permissions).
  - repository_selection (string): all or selected.
  - repositories (array of Repository objects): repositories the token can access when repository_selection is se


