Tool `OpenAPI Explorer:getApiOperation` with Parameter {'id': 'github', 'operationIdOrRoute': 'repos/update-branch-protection'} on OpenAPI Explorer succeeded. Result (summarized from 1395329 tokens): Summary of GitHub v3 REST API endpoint: Update branch protection

General
- API: GitHub v3 REST API (OpenAPI 3.0.3), version 1.1.4
- Base URL: https://api.github.com
- Docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/branches/branch-protection#update-branch-protection

Endpoint
- Method and path: PUT /repos/{owner}/{repo}/branches/{branch}/protection
- Purpose: Update protection rules on a branch.
- Availability: Protected branches are available on public repos with GitHub Free and GitHub Free for organizations, and on public/private repos with GitHub Pro, Team, Enterprise Cloud, and Enterprise Server.
- Permissions: Requires repository admin or owner permissions.
- Tags: repos
- OperationId: repos/update-branch-protection
- Important notes:
  - Passing new arrays for users, teams, and apps replaces their previous values.
  - Combined total of users + apps + teams is limited to 100.
  - Branch name cannot include wildcards; use GraphQL for wildcard patterns.
  - Branch path parameter supports multi-segment names (e.g., feature/x/y).

Path parameters (all required)
- owner (string): Account owner (case-insensitive).
- repo (string): Repository name without .git (case-insensitive).
- branch (string): Branch name (no wildcards; multi-segment allowed).

Request body (application/json, required)
- required_status_checks (object | null): Require status checks before merge. Set null to disable.
  - strict (boolean): Require branch to be up to date before merging.
  - contexts (string[]; deprecated): Names of status checks to require.
  - checks (array of objects): Fine-grained status checks to require.
    - context (string, required): Name of required check.
    - app_id (integer, optional): ID of GitHub App that must provide the check. Omit to auto-select, or pass -1 to allow any app.
  - Required fields within this object: strict, contexts.
- enforce_admins (boolean | null): Enforce configured restrictions for admins. Set true to enforce; null to disable.
- required_pull_request_reviews (object | null): Require PR reviews before merge. Set null to disable.
  - dismissal_restrictions (object): Who can dismiss reviews. For org repos only; omit for personal repos. Pass empty object to disable.
    - users (string[]): User logins with dismissal access.
    - teams (string[]): Team slugs with dismissal access.
    - apps (string[]): App slugs with dismissal access.
  - dismiss_stale_reviews (boolean): Auto-dismiss approvals on new commits.
  - require_code_owner_reviews (boolean): Require code owner reviews.
  - required_approving_review_count (integer): 0–6 (0 means no reviewers required).
  - require_last_push_approval (boolean, default false): Latest push must be approved by someone other than the pusher.
  - bypass_pull_request_allowances (object): Who can bypass PR requirements.
    - users (string[]): User logins allowed to bypass.
    - teams (string[]): Team slugs allowed to bypass.
    - apps (string[]): App slugs allowed to bypass.
- restrictions (object | null): Restrict who can push. For org repos only. Set null to disable.
  - users (string[], required): User logins with push access.
  - teams (string[], required): Team slugs with push access.
  - apps (string[]): App slugs with push access.
- required_linear_history (boolean): Enforce linear history (no merge commits). Default false; repository must allow squash or rebase merging.
- allow_force_pushes (boolean | null): Allow force pushes by writers. Default false; false or null blocks force pushes.
- allow_deletions (boolean): Allow deletion of the protected branch. Default false.
- block_creations (boolean): If true, push restrictions also block creation of new branches unless initiator has push ability. Default false.
- required_conversation_resolution (boolean): Require all code conversations resolved before merging. Default false.
- lock_branch (boolean, default false): Make branch read-only (no pushes).
- allow_fork_syncing (boolean, default false): Allow fork syncing while branch
