Endpoint
- Path: POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/transfer
- Summary: Transfer a repository
- Description:
  - Transfers repository ownership.
  - If transferring a personal repo to another user, the new owner must accept the request.
  - Response contains the original owner; transfer continues asynchronously.
  - More details: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-repository-transfers/
- Tags: repos
- OperationId: repos/transfer
- API docs: https://docs.github.com/rest/repos/repos#transfer-a-repository

Path parameters
- owner (string, required): Account owner of the repository (case-insensitive).
- repo (string, required): Repository name without “.git” (case-insensitive).

Request body (application/json, required)
- Schema (object):
  - new_owner (string, required): Username or organization name to receive the repo.
  - new_name (string, optional): New name for the repository.
  - team_ids (array of integer, optional): IDs of team(s) to add. Only valid for organization-owned repositories.
- Example:
  - {
      "new_owner": "github",
      "team_ids": [12, 345],
      "new_name": "octorepo"
    }

Responses
- 202 Accepted (application/json): Returns a Minimal Repository object. The transfer proceeds asynchronously; the response includes the original owner.

Minimal Repository schema (key fields)
- Identity and basics:
  - id (int64), node_id (string), name (string), full_name (string), private (boolean), description (string, nullable), fork (boolean), visibility (string), default_branch (string)
- URLs (numerous string URL templates/URIs):
