2) Baryon fraction from BAO amplitude: consistent growth parameterization
- Goal: Robustly measure Ωb/Ωm from galaxy clustering, independent of pre-recombination new physics (e.g., Early Dark Energy).
- Method: Modify CAMB by embedding a parameter controlling baryon vs. CDM balance in growth terms; captures pre-recombination baryonic suppression of CDM; EFT of LSS pipeline with HOD-informed priors; validated on noiseless ΛCDM and EDE cosmologies with DESI-like errors.
- Results: Comparable precision to prior splitting templates with reduced systematics; provides clean linear power spectrum parameterization isolating growth physics.
- Impact: Strengthens baryon-fraction–based H0 inference when combined with BBN (Ωb) and Alcock–Paczynski (Ωm); future DESI/Euclid to tighten constraints.
- Area: Cosmology (astro-ph.CO)

3) Convergence and front position for an FKPP-type free boundary problem
- Problem: Free boundary PDE linked to N-BBM hydrodynamic limit; conjectured in FKPP universality class.
- Results: For sufficiently fast-decaying initial data, solution converges to the minimal traveling wave; sharp necessary and sufficient conditions. Precisely determines L_t asymptotics:
  L_t = √2 t − (3/(2√2)) log t + c + o(1).
- Extensions: General β-parameterized free boundary problem with pulled, pushmi-pullyu (critical), and pushed regimes; establishes sharp convergence conditions and front asymptotics in all regimes—first such necessary and sufficient conditions even beyond classical monostable RD.
- Area: Analysis/Probability (math.AP; math.PR)

4) Provable benefits of sinusoidal activation for modular addition
- Expressivity: Sine MLPs achieve width-2 exact realizations for any fixed length m; with bias, width-2 across all lengths. ReLU needs width ∝ m and cannot fit two lengths with different residues mod p simultaneously.
- Generalization: New Natarajan-dimension bound for sine nets; nearly optimal sample complexity Ỹ(O(p)) for ERM with constant width; width-independent margin-based bounds in overparameterized regime.
- Empirics: Sine networks consistently generalize better than ReLU and extrapolate across lengths.
- Area: ML theory (cs.LG; stat.ML)

5) Quantum topological Hochschild homology (qTHH) and annular Khovanov spectra
- Contribution: Define qTHH and build a new stable homotopy refinement of quantum annular Khovanov homology.
- Equivalence: Matches qTHH of spectral Chen–Khovanov tangle bimodules (Lawson–Lipshitz–Sarkar).
- Consistency: Recovers construction of Krushkal et al. (with first and third authors).
- Area: Topology/Algebra (math.GT; math.AT; math.QA)

6) Heuristic for MPS simulation of 2D TFIM dynamics
- Challenge: Out-of-equilibrium dynamics at intermediate/high energy densities generate near-maximal entanglement; full wavefunction storage is prohibitive.
- Method: Estimate observables by rescaling low-bond-dimension MPS results using a factor dependent only on MPS fidelity; accelerates convergence of expectation values.
- Demo: 2D TFIM on 7×8 PBC; max bond dimension χ=4096 on a single NVIDIA A100 GPU; compared to digital quantum processor runs.
- Scope: Broad energy densities; targets observables rather than full state.
