  - Employs biome-specific linear OCS–GPP relationships to derive six OCS uptake flux fields from different GPP datasets; evaluates against two Alaskan ground sites.
  - Optimized NHL plant uptake OCS flux estimated at approximately −247 Gg S per year.

- Implementation and impacts of surface and blowing snow sources of Arctic bromine activation within WRF-Chem 4.1.1 (Marelle et al., 2021, doi:10.1029/2020MS002391)
  - Implemented detailed bromine and chlorine chemistry and two activation pathways: (1) surface snow on sea ice via ozone deposition (Toyota 2011), (2) sea-salt aerosols from sublimated blowing snow (Yang 2008).
