- It’s currently 11:13 pm local time in Seattle (America/Los_Angeles).
- Due to a Google Maps session error in the tools, I couldn’t run live “Open now” filters. To still give you concrete, verifiable options near Kimpton Hotel Monaco (1101 4th Ave), I’ve shortlisted top-rated downtown spots within easy reach, with exact addresses, typical walking distances/directions, and direct Google Maps links so you can verify “Open now” and ratings in one click.

Closest top-rated options (walkable from Kimpton Hotel Monaco)
1) The Capital Grille (steakhouse)
- Address: 1301 4th Ave, Seattle, WA 98101
- Distance and route from hotel: about 0.2 miles, ~4–5 min. Walk north on 4th Ave for ~2–3 blocks; it’s on the right between Union and University.
- Grade/access: Along 4th Ave this stretch is comparatively flat by downtown standards (gentle grade; no hillclimb).
- Verify rating/hours: Google Maps place page: https://maps.google.com/?q=The+Capital+Grille+Seattle
- One‑click walking directions from Kimpton Monaco: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle,1101+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&destination=The+Capital+Grille,1301+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&travelmode=walking

2) Shuckers Oyster Bar (seafood/oysters; in the Fairmont Olympic)
- Address: 411 University St, Seattle, WA 98101
- Distance and route: about 0.1–0.2 miles, ~3–4 min. Walk north on 4th Ave one block to University St; turn left (west) ~100–200 ft.
- Grade/access: Minimal elevation change staying on 4th Ave and University St.
- Verify rating/hours: Google Maps: https://maps.google.com/?q=Shuckers+Oyster+Bar+Seattle
- Directions: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle,1101+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&destination=Shuckers+Oyster+Bar,411+University+St,Seattle,WA&travelmode=walking

3) Wild Ginger (Pan‑Asian)
- Address: 1401 3rd Ave, Seattle, WA 98101 (Benaroya Hall block)
- Distance and route: about 0.2 miles, ~5 min. Go north on 4th Ave ~2 blocks, left on Union St 1 block to 3rd Ave.
- Grade/access: Slight downhill on Union St; still relatively gentle compared with routes to 1st Ave.
- Verify rating/hours: Google Maps: https://maps.google.com/?q=Wild+Ginger+Seattle
- Directions: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle,1101+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&destination=Wild+Ginger,1401+3rd+Ave,Seattle,WA&travelmode=walking

4) Japonessa Sushi Cocina (sushi; late‑night friendly historically)
- Address: 1400 1st Ave, Seattle, WA 98101
- Distance and route: about 0.4 miles, ~8–10 min. Easiest route with fewer steep blocks: north on 4th Ave to Union St, left (west) on Union to 2nd Ave, continue to 1st Ave.
- Grade/access: Notable downhill from 4th Ave to 1st Ave. If grade is a concern, take Union St to 2nd Ave and continue gently to 1st Ave; avoid the steeper Spring/Seneca St blocks.
- Verify rating/hours: Google Maps: https://maps.google.com/?q=Japonessa+Seattle
- Directions: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle,1101+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&destination=Japonessa,1400+1st+Ave,Seattle,WA&travelmode=walking

Alternative classic nearby (note: verify late‑night hours)
- The Metropolitan Grill (steakhouse): 820 2nd Ave, Seattle, WA 98104. ~0.3 miles; route is west on Spring St (downhill) to 2nd Ave, then south to Marion St. Google Maps: https://maps.google.com/?q=Metropolitan+Grill+Seattle. Directions: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&origin=Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle,1101+4th+Ave,Seattle,WA&destination=Metropolitan+Grill,820+2nd+Ave,Seattle,WA&travelmode=walking

Elevation/grade and accessibility notes you can verify
- Downtown slopes downward from 4th Ave toward 1st Ave and the waterfront. Routes that stay on 3rd–4th Ave are generally flatter; routes dropping to 1st Ave are noticeably downhill.
- The City of Seattle’s Downtown Accessible Route Map highlights gentler‑grade corridors, elevators, and hillclimb assists. You can use it to pick the flattest paths from the hotel:
  - Seattle DOT Downtown Accessible Routes (official): https://www.seattle.gov/transportation/projects-and-programs/programs/mobility-programs/accessible-route-maps/downtown-accessible-routes
  - For reaching the waterfront level using ramps/elevators, the Harbor Steps corridor between 1st/2nd Ave provides step‑free options (info: Downtown Seattle Association page): https://downtownseattle.org/visit/things-to-do/harbor-steps/

How to confirm “Open now,” ratings, distance, and elevation in one step
- Live “open now” and ratings (Google Maps):
  - Top‑rated restaurants near Kimpton Monaco: https://www.google.com/maps/search/restaurants+near+Kimpton+Hotel+Monaco+Seattle
  - Once open, tap “Open now” and set “Rating: 4.0+.”
- Exact walking distance and grade:
  - Use the directions links I provided above; Google Maps will show the current walking time and distance for each. If you tap the route options, it will also suggest gentler paths (and you can avoid steeper streets like Spring/Seneca if needed).
- Current local time reference used: Time MCP returned 2025‑11‑26T23:13:17‑08:00 (America/Los_Angeles).

Why these picks (and what to expect)
- All listed restaurants are well‑known downtown mainstays with consistently high public ratings on Google/Yelp (see their Google Maps pages above to verify current star ratings and hours).
- The Capital Grille, Shuckers, and Wild Ginger are the most accessible from Kimpton Monaco with minimal elevation change; Japonessa is excellent but involves a noticeable downhill.

