Important notes on interpreting these numbers
- FIPE is Brazil‑specific and reports average market values per model/trim/year for the reference month. It includes both used and zero‑km (year=32000) prices. If you’re shopping outside Brazil, we should use your local sources instead.
- “Average price for Toyota cars” needs scoping. An average over “all Toyota entries” mixes classic/used and current/zero‑km models, which isn’t decision‑useful. A better approach is:
  1) choose “new (zero‑km) only” and
  2) restrict to models currently on sale and
  3) compute mean/median by segment.

