2025-12-01 11:46:50,382 - agent.executor - INFO -     Tool result: ### Using a Custom Agent with node-fetch (JavaScript)

Source: https://github.com/node-fetch/node-fetch/blob/main/README.md

Illustrates how to provide a custom agent function to the fetch options. This function can return different http.Agent or https.Agent instances based on the URL protocol, allowing for fine-grained control over networking behavior like keep-alive or handling self-signed certificates.

```javascript
import http from 'node:http';
import https from 'node:https';

const httpAgent = new http.Agent({
	keepAlive: true
});
const httpsAgent = new https.Agent({
	keepAlive: true
});

const options = {
	agent: function(_parsedURL) {
		if (_parsedURL.protocol == 'http:') {
			return httpAgent;
		} else {
			return httpsAgent;
		}
	}
};
```

