Installation and module formats
- Install latest (ESM-only, Node ≥12.20): npm install node-fetch
- Install CommonJS-compatible v2: npm install node-fetch@2
- ESM import (v3): import fetch from 'node-fetch'
- CommonJS usage (v3) via dynamic import: const fetch = (...args) => import('node-fetch').then(({default: fetch}) => fetch(...args))
- Optional global polyfill (ESM): Patch globalThis with fetch, Headers, Request, Response for app-wide use

Default options (high level)
- Fetch Standard: method 'GET', headers (Headers-compatible init), body (null or Readable), redirect 'follow', signal null
- Extensions: follow 20, compress true, size 0, agent null (Agent or function), highWaterMark 16384, insecureHTTPParser false

Networking control
- Custom agent per protocol: Provide options.agent = (parsedURL) => http.Agent or https.Agent (e.g., keepAlive)
- Manual redirects: redirect: 'manual', inspect response.status (301/302), read Location header, perform next fetch

Timeouts and cancellation
- Timeout with timeout-signal: fetch(url, { signal: timeoutSignal(ms) }); catch AbortError
- Manual AbortController timeout: create controller, setTimeout(controller.abort, ms), pass signal, catch AbortError; clear timeout in finally
- AbortError detection: error instanceof AbortError (ESM) or error.name === 'AbortError' (CJS examples)

Streams and large responses
- Tune buffering: highWaterMark option controls internal stream buffer size (e.g., 1MB)
- Clone and read in parallel: response.clone(); await Promise.all([response.json(), clone.text()])
- Streaming consumption:
  - Node 14+: for await (const chunk of response.body) { ... }
  - Node 12: attach 'error'/'close' listeners; iterate with for await; wrap completion in a Promise
- Download to file: use stream.pipeline (promisified) to pipe response.body to fs.createWriteStream; check response.ok before piping

Response handling and errors
- Access metadata: response.ok, status, statusText, headers.raw(), headers.get(name)
- HTTP error handling (non-ok): implement helper to throw on !response.ok (e.g., HTTPResponseError), then inspect error.response and body
- Network/operational errors: wrap fetch in try/catch to handle FetchError and other failures
- JSON parsing errors (v3): res.json() throws SyntaxError on invalid JSON (aligns with spec), not FetchError
- Raw headers: response.headers.raw()['set-cookie'] returns array of Set-Cookie lines

Headers usage and upgrades
- Initialize Headers from object, array of [key, value], Map, or another Headers
- v2 behavior changes:
  - Parameters to Headers methods are stringified: null → 'null', undefined → 'undefined' (no throw)
  - Invalid header names/values are rejected (throws)
  - getAll() removed; emulate by headers.get('Multi').split(',')
  - get() for multi-value headers returns comma-joined string (e.g., 'header1,header2'); emulate old “first value” via split(',')[0]

Character encoding (v3)
- res.textConverted() removed; to convert with charset detection:
  - const buf = await res.arrayBuffer(); const text = convertBody(buf, res.headers) using fetch-charset-detection

Requests: common patterns
- GET text/HTML: await response.text()
- GET JSON: await response.json()
- Simple POST (string body): { method: 'POST', body: 'a=1' }
- POST JSON: set headers['Content-Type'] = 'application/json', body = JSON.stringify(obj)
- POST URLSearchParams: body = new URLSearchParams(); Content-Type set automatically
- FormData uploads:
  - Create FormData, set text fields and File/Blob entries; fetch with { method: 'POST', body: formData }
  - Create File/Blob from data: File([Uint8Array], 'name.txt', { type }), or fileFrom/fileFromSync
  - Post a file: const blob = fileFromSync('./input.txt', 'text/plain'); fetch(url, { method: 'POST', body: blob })
  - Append custom Blob-like object to FormData by providing toStringTag, size, and stream()/arrayBuffer()

Parsing incoming Node.js request
