What’s verified from the data sources used
- Coverage (source: DEX Paprika MCP endpoint “getNetworks” from this session): Supported chains include Fantom, Celo, Aptos, Blast, Linea, Ton, Binance Smart Chain, Optimism, ZkSync, Tron, Sonic, Cronos, HyperEVM, Sei, Arbitrum, Base, Avalanche, Solana, Scroll, Botanix, Mantle, Polygon, Sui, Berachain, Unichain, Ronin, Plasma, Ethereum.
- Ecosystem scope (source: DEX Paprika MCP endpoint “getStats” from this session): 29 chains, 182 factories, 18,075,098 pools, 16,127,525 tokens.
- Implication: Your token’s top pools can be located and compared across the above networks and their DEX factories; we can pull recent snapshots and historical series for TVL and volume to quantify shifts.

What I still need to precisely deliver “top liquidity pools for this token lately vs historically”
- Token identifier: the contract address is best (and per-chain if it’s multichain). Symbol alone can be ambiguous.
- Chain(s) to include: e.g., Ethereum only, or multi-chain (Arbitrum, BSC, Base, etc.).
- DEX scope: a specific DEX (e.g., Uniswap, Trader Joe, PancakeSwap) or “all supported.”
- Time windows: e.g., last 7/30/90 days for the historical baseline.
- Quote pair focus (optional): e.g., versus WETH/WBNB, USDC/USDT, or all pairs.

How I will produce the analysis (and the evidence you’ll receive)
- Pool discovery: Enumerate all pools that contain your token on the requested chain(s) and DEX(s). For each pool: pool address, DEX/factory, chain, fee tier, token0/token1, pool type (v2/v3/CL).
- Recent snapshot metrics per pool (with links/sources):
  - Liquidity/TVL (USD) and token reserves
  - 24h and 7d volume (USD)
  - Fees APR (derived from fee tier × volume/TVL)
  - Depth at ±1% price impact (where available for CL pools)
  - LP concentration (top LP share, if available)
  - Source links: pool pages and API endpoints (DEX Paprika pool endpoints, relevant DEX subgraphs, and/or DefiLlama/Dune dashboards for cross-checks)
- Historical comparison:
  - TVL and volume time series for the last 30–90 days
  - Delta vs prior 30-day average and 7-day average
  - Market share shifts: share of total token liquidity and volume by pool and by chain
  - Notable changes: liquidity migrations between fee tiers/pools, bursts in volume, or new pools overtaking legacy ones
- Synthesis:
  - Which pools are currently dominant by TVL and by flow (volume)
  - Whether volume has consolidated into fewer pools or fragmented
  - Fee tier effectiveness (are 0.05%/0.3%/1% pools winning flows?)
  - Any signs of mercenary liquidity or liquidity mining driving transient TVL
- Clear sourcing: Every number accompanied by an API/source reference or a link to the pool/Explorer/analytics page for verification.

Why this step is necessary
- The tools confirmed broad multi-chain coverage but did not yet pull token-specific pool records in this session. Your token’s contract address ensures we query the correct pools (symbols can collide), and the target chains/DEXs bound the search so results are complete and auditable.

What I need from you to proceed now
- Token contract address (and chain). If multichain, list each address per chain.
- Chains to include (e.g., Ethereum only; or Ethereum + Arbitrum + Base + BSC).
- DEX scope (specific DEX names or “all supported”).
- Desired lookback windows (e.g., recent = last 7 days; historical baseline = prior 30/90 days).
- Preferred quote assets/pairs to emphasize (e.g., stable pairs vs WETH).

Once you provide that, I’ll return:
- A ranked list of the top pools with concrete numbers (TVL, 24h/7d volume, fee tier, pool address) and direct source links.
- A concise historical trend summary (where liquidity/volume has shifted) with supporting charts/tables and references.
- Any noteworthy structural changes (new pools attracting flow, liquidity migrations, fee-tier shifts), plus potential implications to execution quality and LP incentives (purely informational, not financial advice).

If you don’t have the contract handy, share the token name/symbol and I can attempt a disambiguated lookup across the supported networks, but confirmation from you will still be required before finalizing results.
