Why this set: It covers the most common UI primitives with featured variants (preferred defaults) and stable versioned items for edit/chat. You can start with these 20–24 icons and expand as needed.

2) How to use them effectively (with concrete, verifiable numbers)

A) Size, stroke, and color (cross-platform defaults from Huge Icons)
- Default icon size is 24 px across web frameworks. Props default to size=24 and strokeWidth=1.5 for stroke icons. Color defaults to currentColor on web and #000000 on React Native.
  - React: size default 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5
  - Vue: size default 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5
  - Angular: size default 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5
  - Svelte: size default 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5
  - React Native: size default 24, color #000000, strokeWidth 1.5
  - Flutter: size default 24.0, color Colors.black
Sources: Huge Icons get_platform_usage for React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, React Native, Flutter.

Practical recommendation:
- Use size=24 and strokeWidth=1.5 as your baseline for stroke styles, and color=currentColor on web to inherit text color. Keep styles consistent across the app.

B) Accessibility and interaction targets (standards with numbers)
- Touch target size:
  - WCAG 2.2 (AA) Target Size (Minimum) is 24 by 24 CSS px (SC 2.5.8).
  - WCAG (AAA) Target Size (Enhanced) is 44 by 44 CSS px (SC 2.5.5). Apple HIG also recommends 44×44 points for tappable controls.
- Contrast for non-text icons:
  - WCAG 2.1/2.2 Non-text Contrast (SC 1.4.11) requires at least 3:1 contrast for graphical objects and UI components.
- Labels and semantics:
  - Provide accessible names for interactive icons via aria-label, or aria-hidden="true" if purely decorative (WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices).
Sources:
  - WCAG 2.2 SC 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum): 24×24 CSS px (AA).
  - WCAG SC 2.5.5 Target Size (AAA): 44×44 CSS px.
  - WCAG SC 1.4.11 Non-text Contrast: 3:1.
  - Apple Human Interface Guidelines: 44×44 pt minimum touch target.
  - Material Design: Standard icon size 24×24 dp; recommended touch target 48×48 dp.

Practical recommendation:
- Render icons at 24 px with at least a 48×48 px clickable/tappable area for comfortable touch (Material), or 44×44 on iOS.
- Ensure non-text icons meet 3:1 contrast against background.
- Pair navigation icons with text labels in primary nav to reduce ambiguity; where you can’t show labels persistently, provide accessible names and tooltips.

C) Visual consistency
- Choose a single stylistic family (e.g., stroke-rounded) for primary UI to avoid mixing visual grammars. Huge Icons provides multiple pro families (stroke-rounded, stroke-sharp, solid, bulk, duotone, twotone). Source: Huge Icons package list in get_platform_usage outputs.
- Use featured variants where available (e.g., settings-02, checkmark-circle-02, home-01) for a balanced default look validated by the library authors.

D) State handling
- The HugeiconsIcon component supports altIcon and showAlt for hover/active/selected transitions without swapping components. Source: get_platform_usage props for each framework.
- Example usage idea: use checkmark-circle-02 as icon and checkmark-badge-02 as altIcon for a “completed” state; toggle showAlt on completion.

3) Cross-framework implementation details (verifiable commands and defaults)

Install the wrapper for your framework and the free icons package. Pro families require auth via .npmrc.

- React
  - Install: npm install @hugeicons/react and (free icons) @hugeicons/core-free-icons
  - Usage: import { HugeiconsIcon } from '@hugeicons/react'; import { Notification03Icon } from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
  - Defaults: size 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5, className supported
  - Props include icon (required), altIcon, showAlt, size, color, strokeWidth, className

- Vue
  - Install: npm install @hugeicons/vue and @hugeicons/core-free-icons
  - Usage: import { HugeiconsIcon } from '@hugeicons/vue'; import { Notification03Icon } from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
  - Defaults: size 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5, class supported

- Angular
  - Install: npm install @hugeicons/angular and @hugeicons/core-free-icons
  - Usage: template uses <hugeicons-icon [icon]="..." [size]="24" color="currentColor" [strokeWidth]="1.5"></hugeicons-icon>
  - Defaults: size 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5

- Svelte
  - Install: npm install @hugeicons/svelte and @hugeicons/core-free-icons
  - Usage: <HugeiconsIcon icon={...} size={24} color="currentColor" strokeWidth={1.5} />
  - Defaults: size 24, color currentColor, strokeWidth 1.5

- React Native
  - Install: npm install @hugeicons/react-native and @hugeicons/core-free-icons
  - Usage: <HugeiconsIcon icon={...} size={24} color="#000000" strokeWidth={1.5} />
  - Defaults: size 24, color #000000, strokeWidth 1.5

- Flutter
  - Install: pubspec dependency hugeicons: ^0.0.10
  - Usage: HugeIcon(icon: HugeIcons.strokeRoundedHome01, size: 30.0, color: Colors.red)
  - Defaults: size 24.0, color Colors.black
Sources: Huge Icons get_platform_usage for React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, React Native, Flutter.

